{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-74350",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have $n=3$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is approximated as \n\n$$\nA≈f(3.5)Δ{x}_{1}+f(4)Δ{x}_{2}+f(6)Δ{x}_{3},\n$$\n\nwhere each $Δ{x}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $x$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\nΔ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $Δx$'s.\n\n| $x$ | $2$ | $3.5$ | $4$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $Δx$ | $-$ | $1.5$ | $0.5$ | $2$ |\n| $f(x)$ | $-$ | $2$ | $3.5$ | $8$ |\n\nFinally, we plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈2\\cdot 1.5+3.5\\cdot 0.5+8\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3+1.75+16 \\\\  & =20.75.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
